<title>UK: UBS sets warrants on 30-year U.S. Treasury. [CORRECTED 13:04 GMT]</title>
<headline>UBS sets warrants on 30-year U.S. Treasury. [CORRECTED 13:04 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>UBS Zurich said it has issued four million European-style call and put warrants, in two equal tranches, on the 6.625 percent U.S. Treasury due February 2027.</p>
<p>(Corrects to make clear that second tranche is a put warrant).</p>
<p>COMMON TERMS:</p>
<p> EXPIRATION	27.OCT.97   PAYDATE   14.MAY.97</p>
<p> LISTING	   NONE	  SPOT REF  96 08/32 (07.MAY.97)</p>
<p>* * * * * * * * *</p>
<p>		     STRIKE	  PRICE</p>
<p> CALL		96 00/32	$4.05</p>
<p> PUT		 96 00/32	$3.53</p>
<p> NOTES   ON EXPIRY THE INVESTOR IS ELIGIBLE TO GET PAYMENT</p>
<p>	   OF THE SQUARED DIFFERENCE BETWEEN SPOT AND STRIKE, IF</p>
<p>	   THE SPOT IS HIGHER THAN THE STRIKE, ELSE THE WARRANT</p>
<p>	   EXPIRES WORTHLESS.</p>
<p>--Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
